# solarsindy.env — optional configuration for bin/solarsindy.
#
# Copy to the clone root and edit:
#   cp deploy/solarsindy.env.example solarsindy.env
#
# bin/solarsindy reads this file before every command. Only simple KEY=VALUE lines are
# honored (comments and blank lines are skipped), and environment variables that are
# already set WIN over the file — the file supplies defaults, so one-off overrides like
# `SWM_PORT=9000 bin/solarsindy start dashboard` always work. The file is gitignored:
# keep secrets like webhook URLs here, never in tracked files.
#
# Set SOLARSINDY_ENV_FILE to load a config from a non-default path instead of this file;
# a value that points at a missing file warns and loads no config (a typo is not silently
# ignored).
#
# Installed services (macOS launchd): a launchd job inherits nothing from an interactive
# shell, so `bin/solarsindy install-service` renders the allow-listed keys below into each
# service's EnvironmentVariables block and prints, at install time, any key that is set but
# reaches none of the selected services. Editing this file after an install does not reach a
# running service — re-run `bin/solarsindy install-service`. Until then `bin/solarsindy
# status` reads the installed plist's port, so it probes the port the service actually binds
# rather than the one written here. Which service reads which key:
#   live monitor  SOLARSINDY_MONITOR_DIR, SOLARSINDY_V2_CALIBRATION, LIVE_MONITOR_*,
#                 LIVE_FUTURE_CLOCK_TOLERANCE_MIN, LIVE_MAX_FUTURE_CLOCK_SKEW_MIN,
#                 SOLARSINDY_V2_4_DEPLOY_DIR, SOLARSINDY_V2_3_SHADOW_DIR,
#                 SOLARSINDY_V2_2_STACK, SOLARSINDY_V2_2_STACK_SHA256,
#                 SOLARSINDY_ALLOW_UNPINNED_STACK
#   dashboard     SWM_HOST, SWM_PORT, SWM_WEBHOOK_URL
#   watchdog      SWM_WEBHOOK_URL, SOLARSINDY_WATCHDOG_* (its health URL follows SWM_HOST/PORT)
#   collector     SOLARSINDY_V22_RECEIPT_DIR, SOLARSINDY_V22_RECEIPT_LOG_DIR
# JULIA, SOLARSINDY_JULIA_THREADS, SOLARSINDY_NO_OPEN and SOLARSINDY_IGNORE_SERVICE apply to
# bin/solarsindy only; the installed plists pin the interpreter and thread counts themselves.

# ---- dashboard ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bind address. Keep 127.0.0.1 unless behind a trusted reverse proxy.
#SWM_HOST=127.0.0.1
#SWM_PORT=8723

# Push alerts (Slack/Discord/generic JSON POST) on threat-level changes and outages.
#SWM_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.example.com/services/...

# ---- forecast daemon ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Instance state directory (forecast log, reports, snapshots, pidfiles, logs).
#SOLARSINDY_MONITOR_DIR=/path/to/SolarSINDy.jl/var/monitor

# Forecast cadence in seconds (default 3600; fixed-rate, drift-free).
#LIVE_MONITOR_INTERVAL_SEC=3600

# Source-clock skew band, in whole minutes. Below the tolerance a future-dated feed sample
# is not remarked on; between the tolerance and the sanity limit it is reported and its
# post-issue samples are excluded as non-causal; beyond the sanity limit issuance fails
# closed. Widen only on a host with known, measured clock drift.
#LIVE_FUTURE_CLOCK_TOLERANCE_MIN=2
#LIVE_MAX_FUTURE_CLOCK_SKEW_MIN=15

# V2 calibration CSV override (default: <monitor dir>/operational_v2_calibration.csv,
# falling back to the bundled locked calibration in deploy/).
#SOLARSINDY_V2_CALIBRATION=/path/to/operational_v2_calibration.csv

# ---- served static V2.2 stack -------------------------------------------------------
# The served point center is the V2.1 operator followed by the fitted static regime stack.
# Weights default to deploy/operational_v2_2_stack.csv and must match the pinned digest in
# deploy/operational_v2_2_stack_manifest.csv; a mismatch serves the V2.1 center and labels the
# row with the V2.1 identity. Override the path only for a staged rollout.
#SOLARSINDY_V2_2_STACK=/path/to/operational_v2_2_stack.csv
# Override the expected digest only when staging a re-fit.
#SOLARSINDY_V2_2_STACK_SHA256=66e7347f71f5cdf407e85d4612702bb19c82dcbcd74d8c79526173f839472d7d
# An empty digest override removes the only check that ties the weights to the fitted stack the served
# identity names, because the label check passes for any file that copies the label. Such a
# configuration is refused: the row is served by the V2.1 operator and says
# `v2_2_status=fallback_v2_1:stack_unpinned`. Setting the flag below serves the unpinned weights
# instead, under the separate `...+unpinned` identity, which neither the dashboard nor the readiness
# audit accepts as the published product. For staging only.
#SOLARSINDY_ALLOW_UNPINNED_STACK=1

# ---- V2.4 served bundle -------------------------------------------------------------
# The served point center is the V2.4e super-learner over the ten experts, the static V2.2 stack
# among them. Its bundle defaults to deploy/v2_4/ and is verified on load (manifest digests, rebuilt
# analog archive, stack-weight expert set, floor and mass, conformal completeness, guard record).
# Point this elsewhere to serve a different build, or at a nonexistent directory to fall back down
# the chain: the row then carries `v24_status=fallback:deployment_absent` and the static-stack label.
#SOLARSINDY_V2_4_DEPLOY_DIR=/path/to/v2_4

# ---- V2.3 shadow deployment ---------------------------------------------------------
# The V2.3 analog driver continuation is logged as a shadow forecast and never served. Its
# artifacts default to deploy/v2_3_shadow/; point this elsewhere to monitor a different build, or
# at a nonexistent directory to disable the shadow columns.
#SOLARSINDY_V2_3_SHADOW_DIR=/path/to/v2_3_shadow

# ---- V2.2 research receipt collector ---------------------------------------------
# These paths are used only when the explicit `collector` launchd service is
# rendered. The collector is not part of the default service installation.
# A collector-containing install renders only unless SOLARSINDY_LOAD=1 is set.
#SOLARSINDY_V22_RECEIPT_DIR=/path/to/immutable/v2_2_l1_receipts
#SOLARSINDY_V22_RECEIPT_LOG_DIR=/path/to/v2_2_l1_collector_logs

# ---- runtime -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Julia launcher (default: ~/.juliaup/bin/julia if present, else `julia` on PATH).
#JULIA=/usr/local/bin/julia

# Julia threads for the daemons (defaults: monitor 2, dashboard 4).
#SOLARSINDY_JULIA_THREADS=4

# Disable the browser auto-open that `start` performs in interactive terminals.
#SOLARSINDY_NO_OPEN=1

# Advanced: allow a deliberate second CLI instance next to an installed service
# (requires a distinct SWM_PORT *and* SOLARSINDY_MONITOR_DIR).
#SOLARSINDY_IGNORE_SERVICE=1
